there is some good news among all the  pain and suffering we've shown you for  the past three weeks now a nevada couple  is home after spending 10 days on the  ground in ukraine they hope you can help  them in their mission to give the  ukrainian people a better life in a  completely new country our david sharon  spoke to them from their home in carson  city  i said let's go let's go roll up our  sleeves and help people  and that's exactly what we did army  veteran john staub and his wife lydia  karasinska say it took just seconds to  decide they'd help ukrainian refugees on  the polish border it's really close to  home to me it's very personal personal  because karasinska is from poland and  has friends in ukraine  since the start of war three weeks ago  three million refugees have sought  shelter many in neighboring poland i  don't think anything really  can  describe  even words can describe really what is  going on there photos can give you a  glimpse of what it is like  videos maybe can do better job but  it's really hard to do so  the couple spending 10 days on the  ground taking videos when they could of  the thousands of women and children  trying to flee to safety they slept in  sleeping bags on the ground the  temperature at night falling well below  freezing there is a really big risk of  hypothermia which actually  10 children died  before we got there  so it's  you don't really think about your own  safety when you hear stories like that  they crossed the border 19 times even  spending 11 thousand dollars to buy an  ambulance they say that will help  transport people supplies and food so  it's the duty of us as citizens of the  world  to come to their aid and protect them  through this this terrible conflict now  back in nevada they hope to raise money  for ukrainians who are calling poland  home those forced to leave their lives  behind and create new ones  safe from war  i'm david charns live local now  the couple has started an organization  called ukrainian refugee rescue you can  find a link to help on our website at  8newsnow.com
 

